WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.394 --> 00:00:16.219
"Wow!" Perda thought when she saw Zira's mansion.

2
00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:18.861
"Things have changed since I left!"

3
00:00:18.881 --> 00:00:22.543
"Zira made her house even bigger," Zann said.

4
00:00:22.563 --> 00:00:23.663
"And look!

5
00:00:24.184 --> 00:00:26.365
There are fancy houses all around now."

6
00:00:27.165 --> 00:00:31.788
The humble shacks of Zira's closest neighbors had been replaced by large houses.

7
00:00:32.628 --> 00:00:37.471
"I wonder if other people are figuring out how to use magic," Perda said hopefully.

8
00:00:37.491 --> 00:00:40.153
"That would be a good thing for Terrica."

9
00:00:41.554 --> 00:00:44.716
Vilkor was nearby, heading toward Zira's front door.

10
00:00:45.297 --> 00:00:47.518
When he heard Perda's comment, he laughed.

11
00:00:51.381 --> 00:00:53.883
be silly," Vilkor said.

12
00:00:53.903 --> 00:01:01.568
"Only a few trusted and worthy people know the secret of He glanced around and lowered his voice.

13
00:01:02.444 --> 00:01:04.786
"Friction." "I see."

14
00:01:05.287 --> 00:01:06.027
Perda frowned.

15
00:01:06.047 --> 00:01:09.990
"So you and Zira are still hoarding all the magic power."

16
00:01:10.751 --> 00:01:11.572
Vilkor shrugged.

17
00:01:11.592 --> 00:01:12.733
"Why not?

18
00:01:13.053 --> 00:01:14.574
That's how the world works.

19
00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:17.917
Some people have power, and some don't."

20
00:01:19.338 --> 00:01:20.159
He went inside.

21
00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:24.462
"Let's go in and see if Mellis and Zing are safe," Zann said.

22
00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:28.005
The front door opened into an enormous reception room.

23
00:01:28.606 --> 00:01:34.177
Zira was seated in a throne-like chair at the center, with several goons standing guard beside her.

24
00:01:35.057 --> 00:01:39.018
People in fancy clothes were sitting on sofas or chatting with one another.

25
00:01:39.838 --> 00:01:41.719
Perda didn't see Mellis or Zing though.

26
00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:47.501
Zira was talking with one of the goons, but she looked up when Vilkor strutted toward her.

27
00:01:47.521 --> 00:01:50.381
"Oh, you're back."

28
00:01:51.322 --> 00:01:53.522
She didn't sound particularly pleased.

29
00:01:54.703 --> 00:01:56.863
"Yes, and we need to talk."

30
00:01:57.663 --> 00:01:59.404
Vilkor put his hands on his hips.

31
00:02:00.124 --> 00:02:05.806
"It has come to my attention that you might be trying to take over this whole operation.

32
00:02:06.527 --> 00:02:11.549
I've been suspicious ever since you shared our secret with that shifty Krub."

33
00:02:12.529 --> 00:02:13.390
Zira smirked.

34
00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:17.231
"So you're worried about losing a little power, are you?

35
00:02:17.952 --> 00:02:20.693
You're afraid I'll kick you out of the inner circle?

36
00:02:21.453 --> 00:02:22.233
Oh, dear."

37
00:02:23.154 --> 00:02:28.416
She snapped her fingers to create a large fireball, which she flung lazily in Vilkor's direction.

38
00:02:29.216 --> 00:02:29.876
He dodged it.

39
00:02:29.896 --> 00:02:32.578
"Hey! You could have burned me!"

40
00:02:33.198 --> 00:02:36.380
"She created that fireball so easily," Zann whispered.

41
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.401
"It reminds me of Morb.

42
00:02:39.462 --> 00:02:42.063
Nobody believed that a Void could have that much power."

43
00:02:42.784 --> 00:02:44.625
Perda thought about what Zann had said.

44
00:02:44.645 --> 00:02:49.748
"Yes, Zira seems powerful and scary," she murmured.

45
00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:56.532
"Still, most of the magic she uses is flashy but fairly easy to counteract.

46
00:02:57.496 --> 00:03:01.480
For instance, I had no trouble zapping out of that Compel spell."

47
00:03:03.321 --> 00:03:04.662
Zann nodded thoughtfully.

48
00:03:04.682 --> 00:03:06.024
"I see what you mean.

49
00:03:06.724 --> 00:03:11.048
That fireball looked impressive, but it didn't even come close to hitting Vilkor."

50
00:03:11.068 --> 00:03:14.791
"Zira is quick and clever about learning magic.

51
00:03:15.372 --> 00:03:19.936
But maybe she's not quite as powerful as she's making herself seem."

52
00:03:20.717 --> 00:03:21.718
Perda stepped forward.

53
00:03:21.738 --> 00:03:23.279
"Hey, Zira!"

54
00:03:23.759 --> 00:03:24.260
she shouted.

55
00:03:24.736 --> 00:03:27.497
"You have no right to hold Mellis prisoner.

56
00:03:28.457 --> 00:03:33.298
We demand that you release her—along with the dragon—right away!"

57
00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:37.080
Zira frowned when she saw Perda and Zann.

58
00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.840
"How did you—?

59
00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:40.861
Oh, never mind.

60
00:03:41.741 --> 00:03:45.222
I have no time to deal with bratty children right now."

61
00:03:46.082 --> 00:03:48.963
She clapped her hands to create several large fireballs.

62
00:03:49.663 --> 00:03:53.144
Perda didn't flinch as they came toward her and Zann.

63
00:03:53.164 --> 00:03:59.926
Instead, she snapped her fingers and created a glowing purple shield that easily repelled the missiles, causing them

64
00:03:59.966 --> 00:04:01.567
to bounce back toward Zira.

65
00:04:01.587 --> 00:04:06.168
"Hey!" Zira ducked, falling out of her throne.

66
00:04:06.928 --> 00:04:10.389
The goons also dodged the fireballs, shouting with dismay.

67
00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:15.451
One of them didn't move quite fast enough and ended up with a singed shoulder.

68
00:04:15.471 --> 00:04:19.032
"Get ready," Perda whispered to Zann.

69
00:04:19.052 --> 00:04:23.255
"She'll try to scare us, but just remember that we know more magic than she does."

70
00:04:24.136 --> 00:04:26.878
Zann nodded, rubbing his hands together vigorously.

71
00:04:26.898 --> 00:04:29.820
"Join friction," he whispered back.

72
00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.942
Perda held out her shackled hands, and Zann started rubbing them.

73
00:04:34.563 --> 00:04:37.765
Within seconds, magic energy was crackling around them.

74
00:04:37.785 --> 00:04:41.107
"That wasn't funny," Zira snarled.

75
00:04:41.127 --> 00:04:45.270
"You'll be sorry you tried to humiliate me."

76
00:04:46.031 --> 00:04:47.292
She rubbed her hands together.

77
00:04:47.984 --> 00:04:51.166
Angry red smoke appeared, billowing away from Zira.

78
00:04:51.806 --> 00:04:54.087
People coughed and fainted as it reached them.

79
00:04:55.108 --> 00:04:56.028
Perda thought quickly.

80
00:04:56.709 --> 00:04:58.090
"Rain!" she said.

81
00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:04.093
Sheets of water poured down from the ceiling, beating down the smoke until it disappeared.

82
00:05:04.773 --> 00:05:10.936
The people who were still conscious ran around in confusion or crawled under the furniture to protect themselves

83
00:05:10.997 --> 00:05:11.777
from the downpour.

84
00:05:12.557 --> 00:05:14.979
Zira snapped her fingers to create an umbrella.

85
00:05:15.519 --> 00:05:17.180
Then she strode forward.

86
00:05:17.836 --> 00:05:20.638
"Don't be cowards, kids," she said.

87
00:05:20.658 --> 00:05:24.160
"Face me without your silly magical wall."

88
00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.241
"Sure, why not?"

89
00:05:27.101 --> 00:05:30.023
Perda snapped her fingers, and the shield disappeared.

90
00:05:30.903 --> 00:05:31.624
So did the rain.

91
00:05:32.544 --> 00:05:33.745
"We're not afraid of you."

92
00:05:33.765 --> 00:05:35.626
"You should be."

93
00:05:36.406 --> 00:05:37.627
Zira rubbed her hands.

94
00:05:38.347 --> 00:05:42.390
An enormous fireball appeared, almost as big as Zira herself.

95
00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:46.332
As it flew toward her and Zann, Perda sighed loudly.

96
00:05:47.052 --> 00:05:50.053
"Don't you know how to do anything else?"

97
00:05:50.894 --> 00:05:51.554
she commented.

98
00:05:51.574 --> 00:05:55.055
"I mean, really—this is getting boring."

99
00:05:55.876 --> 00:05:59.417
She used a Deflect spell to send the fireball spinning upward.

100
00:06:00.137 --> 00:06:03.739
Then she used a Levitation spell to lift Zira off her feet.

101
00:06:04.439 --> 00:06:08.081
The woman dangled in the air, her eyes wide with alarm.

102
00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:10.442
"Put me down!"

103
00:06:10.982 --> 00:06:11.642
Zira shouted.

104
00:06:12.322 --> 00:06:13.123
Perda obeyed.

105
00:06:13.943 --> 00:06:17.749
As soon as the woman's feet touched the floor, Zira clapped her hands.

106
00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.531
Right away a gorzog appeared.

107
00:06:20.551 --> 00:06:22.793
"Whoa!" Zann cried.

108
00:06:22.813 --> 00:06:25.475
"I thought you couldn't create animals with magic!"

109
00:06:26.255 --> 00:06:26.956
"You can't."

110
00:06:27.656 --> 00:06:31.219
Perda could see that the gorzog looked surprised and confused.

111
00:06:31.239 --> 00:06:35.322
"Zira just transported it here from somewhere else."

112
00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:40.305
The gorzog regained its senses enough to snarl and leap toward Perda.

113
00:06:41.126 --> 00:06:42.066
But Perda was ready.

114
00:06:42.086 --> 00:06:44.008
"Cage," she thought.

115
00:06:44.732 --> 00:06:50.174
A sturdy cage formed around the creature in midair and then crashed to the floor.

116
00:06:50.374 --> 00:06:51.595
Zira looked surprised.

117
00:06:51.995 --> 00:06:53.235
But she recovered quickly.

118
00:06:53.255 --> 00:06:57.117
"Ah, well done," she said smoothly.

119
00:06:57.137 --> 00:07:00.418
"You've proven yourselves and passed my test."

120
00:07:01.119 --> 00:07:02.639
She turned toward Vilkor.

121
00:07:02.659 --> 00:07:06.441
"It was wise of you to bring them here, my trusted friend."

122
00:07:07.461 --> 00:07:08.882
Vilkor tilted his head.

123
00:07:08.902 --> 00:07:11.763
"Huh?" Zira ignored him.

124
00:07:12.283 --> 00:07:14.184
She turned back to Zann and Perda.

125
00:07:14.937 --> 00:07:16.865
"Welcome to the inner circle,
